    "lang": "c",
    "pr_title": "Bluetooth: Audio: Make PACS optional notify actually optional",
    "pr_body": "Added KConfig options to make the various PACS characteristics that are optionally notifiable selectable as notifiable. Selecting a characteristic as notifiable will make it so for all pacs instances on the device.\r\n\r\nFixes https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/issues/56456",
    "pr_comments": [
        "> I expect this to heavily conflict with #55572. I suggest to get the #55572 in first, and then update this PR afterwards.\r\n> \r\n> This PR also partially fixes #57473, but does not contain support for subscribing in the client implementation.\r\n\r\nIll wait for this one and update once its in",
        "@fredrikdanebjer This can now be rebased and be marked ready for review :) ",
        "@szymon-czapracki I'd urge you specifically to take a look at this patch, as it makes quite some changes to your recently merged PR https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/pull/55572",
        "> I would also strongly suggest to update the babblesim tests to verify this new behavior\r\n\r\nThis a good point. Ill take a look at this asap also"
    ],
    "merged": true,
    "created_at": "2023-07-11T08:44:06Z",
    "issue_context": {
        "number": 57473,
        "title": "LE Audio: PACS optional notification support",
        "body": "**Is your enhancement proposal related to a problem? Please describe.**\r\nMost of the PACS characteristics are optionally notifiable which should be reflected in the implementations. \r\n\r\n**Describe the solution you'd like**\r\nThe PACS implementation should optionally support sending notifications for the characteristics. \r\n\r\nThe BAP Unicast Client implemenation should optionally support subscribing to these as well as handling the notifications. \r\n\r\n**Describe alternatives you've considered**\r\nN/A\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\nN/A\r\n",
        "comments": [
            "https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/pull/57731 fixes this for the PACS server, but the unicast client support is still missing\n\n"
        ]
    },
